wildos-winmode (0.3.15) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Opening a Windows app while Windows is paused no longer starts a new
    connection each time. Remote Desktop ended the connection soon after
    the last app closed (measured on an XPS 13: the next Word took 10.7 s,
    4.5 s of it connecting again and Windows restarting its RemoteApp
    shell, and Word started cold as only an open connection's launches
    use the warm copy). wild-guest --start now stays, with no window, for
    as long as its connection, so it stays open through pauses (tested:
    90 s after the last app closed, and through a 3 minute pause). The
    one a newer connection starts ends the one before.
  * Each start carries a one-time "once", and wild-guest starts it a
    single time: a connection that reconnects by itself no longer opens
    its first app again.
  * wild-guest updates itself in a Windows that is already set up: after
    a minute with no app open, Windows mode compares it with this
    package's copy (state "guest_exe", which setup and an install record)
    and puts the new one in before pausing. Before, a wild-guest fix only
    reached new setups. Tested on the WSL test Windows.

