wildos-winmode (0.3.14) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The first Windows app after the PC restarts opens in seconds: with no
    Windows app open, Windows is now saved to disk as the PC shuts down,
    restarts or updates, instead of shut down. Measured on an XPS 13 9310,
    a start from off took 104 s for Windows to boot (82 s to Remote
    Desktop, 108 s to Word); loading back from disk takes about 5 s. A PC
    shut down while Windows was still starting no longer cuts it off part
    way, which had made its next start slower still. It shuts down only
    when a new memory limit or a fresh sign-in needs it.
  * Windows still restarts to finish its updates, in the background: when
    no app has been open for a minute and the PC is on mains, Windows mode
    asks Windows (at most hourly) whether an update waits for a restart,
    or whether it last restarted a week or more ago, and if so shuts it
    down cleanly and starts it again ahead of time. An app opened
    meanwhile waits for it, as from off.
  * Starting from off says so plainly, with a minute or two expected
    (90 s until this PC has timed it), and that it only happens now and
    then.

