wildos-winmode (0.3.13) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Setting up Windows mode puts problems right by itself. Before each
    step it checks that what the step needs is there and makes again
    whatever has gone, such as the setup disc, which used to make Try
    again fail at once. A step that fails is tried again; if it fails
    twice, what it made is cleared and setup goes back a step. Only if
    that fails twice too does setup stop and offer Try again and Start
    over. Your documents and shared folders are never touched.
  * A PC that restarts while Windows is still copying itself starts the
    install again cleanly, instead of waiting two hours on a disk that
    can't start.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000

wildos-winmode (0.3.12) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Windows desktop opens again after its window was closed. FreeRDP could
    stay running with no window after Windows showed an error, and the
    button then did nothing until the PC restarted. Restarting, shutting
    down or saving Windows mode now ends the desktop too.
  * Remove Windows mode works: after an administrator's password, Windows,
    its programs, their Start entries and file types, the saved sign-in
    and everything setup downloaded are deleted, and Windows mode is ready
    to set up again. Documents in the shared folders are not touched.
  * Windows set up again (Start over, or after Remove) is trusted on the
    first connection. FreeRDP refused it because its certificate differed
    from the last Windows', so no app could open.
  * Windows keeps its Windows mode account a local one. Signing in to a
    Microsoft account from activation's troubleshooter turned the account
    into a Microsoft account, after which Windows refused Windows mode's
    password ("The username or password is incorrect"). Office and the
    Store still sign in to Microsoft accounts for themselves.

