wildos-winmode (0.3.11) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A USB device that only works with Windows, such as a licence dongle,
    label printer or scanner, can be handed to Windows from Settings >
    Windows apps > Windows mode, and given back with the same switch.
    The choice is remembered for that device, so it goes to Windows
    whenever Windows is running and it is plugged in, and comes back to
    Wild OS when Windows stops. Keyboards, mice, touchpads and the drive
    Wild OS runs from are never offered, and a device USB protection has
    blocked stays blocked until it is allowed. Giving a device to Windows
    asks for an administrator's password.
  * Windows set up from now on has room for seven USB devices at once
    instead of three.

