wildos-winmode (0.3.10) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Microsoft Store apps (the new Outlook, WhatsApp, Teams, Microsoft 365
    from the Store and the like) get Start entries with their own icons
    and open like other Windows apps. wild-guest's session helper lists
    the Start menu's packaged apps from the Shell's Applications folder,
    and starts one by its app id through Windows' own activation, whether
    a launch names its program or its shell:AppsFolder address, including
    as the first app of a RemoteApp connection.
  * A Store app that Windows opens in a frame (Calculator, Settings) is
    known as that app once its window is open, so it shows as open and
    groups with its own icon, instead of as a window of Windows itself:
    wild-guest names the app inside the frame by its app id.
  * wild-guest is stricter about what Wild OS's requests may name. Icons
    are read only from local disks outside other accounts' profiles,
    launches and warm apps only name programs on a drive letter or by
    name, never \\server\share paths, URLs or protocol handlers, and a
    Start menu shortcut pointing at a network share is skipped. A request
    nested too deeply no longer ends the service, a failing request no
    longer drops the channel, and only wild-guest itself, in the Windows
    mode account's session, is taken as a session helper.

